/div> </div> </div> </div>I ve calculated that in three turns (of touch with level 2, at distance with level 3) an armored target would start to have serious problems, with the armor almost too hot to be removed by hand.<br /> So yes, it could be lethal to heavy armored opponents, within minutes it could also melt iron items.<br /> <br /> It must be said that it is more limited than the Spagyria Alembic, and in three turns Arc would do much more damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 01-07-2021, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}